brates are effective in managing hypertriglyceridemia, functioning as agonists of the PPAR-α receptor, which plays a crucial role in lipid metabolism. However, it is important to note that fibrates can have gastrointestinal side effects and are contraindicated in individuals with advanced liver and kidney disease.", "PLACENTA:The placenta is an organ that provides nutrients and oxygen to the fetus and secretes hormones during pregnancy.", "FETO:The fetus is the developing offspring in the womb that relies on the mother for nutrients and energy.", "RESISTENCIA A LA INSULINA:\"RESISTENCIA A LA INSULINA\" es una condición metabólica que se caracteriza por una disminución en la capacidad del cuerpo para utilizar la insulina de manera efectiva. Esta condición puede aumentar durante el embarazo, lo que afecta la captación de glucosa y el metabolismo de la madre. Además, la resistencia a la insulina también puede presentarse en pacientes críticamente enfermos, impactando negativamente su metabolismo. Asimismo, se ha observado que este trastorno metabólico puede ocurrir en pacientes con cáncer, lo que repercute en su nutrición y salud general. En resumen, la resistencia a la insulina es un fenómeno que puede afectar a diferentes grupos de pacientes, incluyendo a mujeres embarazadas y aquellos con enfermedades graves, como el cáncer.", "VOLUMEN PLASMÁTICO:Cantidad de plasma en la sangre que aumenta significativamente durante el embarazo.", "CALCIURIA:Calciuria refers to the presence of calcium in the urine, a condition that can influence calcium availability for fetal development. It is characterized by the excretion of calcium in the urine, which tends to increase during pregnancy. This heightened excretion may have implications for both maternal and fetal health, particularly in ensuring adequate calcium levels for the developing fetus.", "HORMONAS DIABETOGÉNICAS:", "WOMEN'S HEALTH INITIATIVE:The Women's Health Initiative is a long-term national health study focused on addressing the most common causes of death, disability, and poor quality of life in postmenopausal women. This initiative investigates various health issues pertinent to this demographic, including the relationship between protein intake and frailty. Through its comprehensive approach, the Women's Health Initiative aims to enhance the understanding of health challenges faced by postmenopausal women and improve their overall well-being.", "HORMONE REPLACEMENT THERAPY:Hormone replacement therapy with estrogens is used in postmenopausal women to seek cardiovascular benefits but has associated risks."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}